b-250240dc4a59" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432053 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432024 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432053 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432025 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432053 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432031 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432053 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432043 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432053 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432050 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432053 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432053 1077 "selection" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432053 1078 #edb/ref 17592186432025 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432053 1079 #uuid "d34edc72-08f2-5a09-a869-52843437095c" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432054 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432027 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432054 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432029 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432054 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432039 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432054 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432040 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432054 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432045 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432054 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432054 1077 "selection" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432054 1078 #edb/ref 17592186432027 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432054 1079 #uuid "d3dc5651-5264-5a29-88a8-48b8aceed863" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432022 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432032 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432035 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432041 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432048 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432055 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432055 1077 "selection" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432055 1078 #edb/ref 17592186432032 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432055 1079 #uuid "e23b2bd8-34af-5d2b-ade2-34acee35a91f" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432056 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432021 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432056 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432026 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432056 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432033 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432056 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432036 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432056 1075 #edb/ref 17592186432049 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432056 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432056 1077 "selection" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432056 1078 #edb/ref 17592186432036 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432056 1079 #uuid "f2c231ef-5289-5db7-b09f-259aa2d1f08e" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432057 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432056 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432057 1069 "q-109523" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432057 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432057 1071 "The random variable $X$ represents the number of foreign ships arriving daily at port $A,$ and the random variable $Y$ is the number of foreign ships arriving daily at port $B.$ The probability distributions of $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nCalculate the expected number of foreign ships arriving at both ports per day." 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432057 1072 #uuid "1c83b6b2-8cdb-5214-8b06-fddb32644de4" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432057 1074 "We need to calculate $\\text{E}[X+Y].$\n\nRecall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables (not necessarily independent), and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nThe expected values of $X$ and $Y$ are calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot 0.1+1\\cdot 0.5+2\\cdot 0.2+3\\cdot 0.2=1.5 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & =0\\cdot 0.5+1\\cdot 0.3+2\\cdot 0.2=0.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X+Y]=\\text{E}[X]+\\text{E}[Y]=1.5+0.7=2.2.\n$$" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432058 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432051 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432058 1069 "q-84114" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432058 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432058 1071 "Compute $\\text{E}[2A+5B]$ if $\\text{E}[A]=-0.5$ and $\\text{E}[B]=0.4.$" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432058 1072 #uuid "5c7770c4-cc2d-59e3-b961-52e126102cc7" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432058 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables (not necessarily independent), and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2A+5B] & =2\\text{E}[A]+5\\text{E}[B] \\\\  & =2(-0.5)+5(0.4) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432059 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432053 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432059 1069 "q-84119" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432059 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432059 1071 "Compute $\\text{E}[6X-4Z]$ if $\\text{E}[X]=2$ and $\\text{E}[Z]=2.$" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432059 1072 #uuid "6027249a-4549-596f-8431-62871ac4f14f" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432059 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables (not necessarily independent), and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[6X-4Z] & =6\\text{E}[X]-4\\text{E}[Z] \\\\  & =6(2)-4(2) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432060 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432052 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432060 1069 "q-108557" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432060 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432060 1071 "For the random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{E}[X]=4$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=5.$ Find $\\text{E}[XY].$" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432060 1072 #uuid "71672eae-2331-5c0a-933f-85ee828fb39f" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432060 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are *independent* random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\cdot Y]=\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y]\n$$\n\nIn this case, however, we don't know whether $X$ and $Y$ are independent. Therefore, $\\text{E}[XY]$ is impossible to determine using only the given information." 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432061 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432054 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432061 1069 "q-127990" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432061 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432061 1071 "The random variable $X$ represents the age of a randomly selected child from a football team, and the random variable $Y$  represents the age of a randomly selected child from a baseball team. The probability distributions of $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$11$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$13$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$11$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.55$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nOne child is selected at random from each team. Calculate the expected sum of ages of the two children." 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432061 1072 #uuid "bb9379fc-94d7-554c-91be-7390d9b4d8c5" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432061 1074 "We need to calculate $\\text{E}[X+Y].$\n\nRecall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables (not necessarily independent), and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nThe expected values of $X$ and $Y$ are calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =10\\cdot 0.1+11\\cdot 0.2+12\\cdot 0.35+13\\cdot 0.35=11.95 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & =10\\cdot 0.2+11\\cdot 0.25+12\\cdot 0.55=11.35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X+Y]=\\text{E}[X]+\\text{E}[Y]=11.95+11.35=23.3.\n$$" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432062 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432055 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432062 1069 "q-109349" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432062 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432062 1071 "For the independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{E}[X]=5$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=0.6.$ Find $\\text{E}[XY].$" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432062 1072 #uuid "f7e9fbd8-7003-5d39-9b68-8eea275c407a" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true] [17592186432062 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are *independent* random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\cdot Y]=\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y]\n$$\n\nSince $X$ and $Y$ are independent, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\cdot Y]=\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y]=5\\cdot 0.6=3.\n$$" 13194139534671 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-07711760-4d84-5bf1-aeae-3f76e11395e1" 17592186432021 "answer-0bc88e36-dea8-5f2b-918d-a47448bd8357" 17592186432022 "answer-162c5f57-a9f7-53b8-b1b6-a0fc170863c8" 17592186432023 "answer-16cf25d3-3fb6-57df-8d11-0f924a53ee27" 17592186432024 "answer-17daf1a4-33c1-5939-b054-77beedb8860e" 17592186432025 "answer-3e4416a7-c43c-57eb-a040-a40e34d1544e" 17592186432026 "answer-421fad1d-d69f-5891-8cc7-ecd706d5a9a6" 17592186432027 "answer-4ceaed98-0bbd-5176-a144-a357ebbf538f" 17592186432028 "answer-5dcc713b-da30-5b10-aa86-0d87c3de5ade" 17592186432029 "answer-621a58ba-7550-520e-a1c2-bd6e7f8b1076" 17592186432030 "answer-661aba9a-91d3-550a-ba62-78837217c25f" 17592186432031 "answer-6a9fd281-dd69-52dc-a834-e9b4ad2064f2" 17592186432032 "answer-78ea3679-b1e5-565c-9b6d-5721d6fd07ea" 17592186432033 "answer-790957d5-7b02-5a48-b8e5-2947b0bb92f4" 17592186432034 "ans